# Trivy waivers for the AGENT image scan (P19 — Jenkinsfile.agent).
#
# DELIBERATELY SEPARATE from the backend `.trivyignore`: the agent image ships the full
# BYOK provider set (`uv sync --extra llm` — anthropic/google-genai/boto3 + their
# transitive deps), a different surface from the backend (`--extra bedrock`). A waiver
# that's justified for one image must NOT silently apply to the other, so each image
# carries its own ignore file.
#
# CI security policy (the Trivy stage runs
# `--severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed --exit-code 1`):
#   * The pipeline FAILS on any HIGH/CRITICAL vulnerability that HAS AN AVAILABLE FIX
#     (remediate-not-waive: bump the base image or the dependency — e.g. the
#     `cryptography>=48.0.1` floor in pyproject.toml's `llm` extra).
#   * Unfixed OS-package advisories (no patched version published yet) are reported but
#     do NOT block a release — `--ignore-unfixed` handles them; the moment a fix ships
#     the gate fails again.
#
# Reserved for SPECIFIC, DOCUMENTED per-CVE waivers (a fixed-but-deliberately-deferred
# advisory). Each entry MUST carry a CVE id, a reason, and a recheck date.
#
# (currently none)
